{"term":"gist","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ed02fbcd371523945f","definition":"The main idea or substance, or the most essential part, of a longer or more complicated matter; the crux, the heart, the pith.","example":"I don't wanna belabor my point; I'm sure you get the gist.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["essence","quintessence","thrust"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gist#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d3e6deff4306e8db6e","definition":"The essential ground for action in a lawsuit, without which there is no cause of action; the gravamen.","example":"[T]heſe charges, of a traiterous or felonious intent, are the points and very giſt of the indictment, and muſt be anſvvered directly, by the general negative, not guilty; […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bowels","sum","brass tacks","core","crux","essence","gist","drift","guts","gravamen","heart","heart and soul","heartstring","heartstrings","inwardness","kernel","marrow","meat","moral of the story","nitty-gritty","nub","nuts and bolts","pith","punctum saliens","quintessence","soul","spirit","stuff","substance","tenor"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"dated","register":"countable, dated","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gist#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:617f5ed6385eaefc74","definition":"Gossip, rumour; (countable) an instance of this.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bowels","sum","brass tacks","core","crux","essence","gist","drift","guts","gravamen","heart","heart and soul","heartstring","heartstrings","inwardness","kernel","marrow","meat","moral of the story","nitty-gritty","nub","nuts and bolts","pith","punctum saliens","quintessence","soul","spirit","stuff","substance","te